In-pane recovery action

Status: DONE
Milestone: Re-snip directly from an invalid-source pane
Dependencies: 03_DESKTOP_CONTROLS.todo
Purpose: Make the source-resized/closed message actionable without finding controls.

Tasks:
- [x] Draw a compact Snip again action inside resized/closed-source placeholders.
- [x] Wire real pointer, focus/keyboard, capture cancellation and selection paths.
- [x] Temporarily suspend click-through for actionable recovery placeholders.
- [x] Preserve the placeholder when selection is cancelled after resize/closure.
- [x] Run native regression checks and inspect the owned recovery screenshot.
- [x] Update user documentation, evidence, ledger and owned continuity.

Acceptance criteria:
- Clicking Snip again opens selection without introducing normal-view chrome.
- Enter/Space activate recovery; releasing a press outside does not activate.
- A minimum-sized pane retains a usable compact action.
- Click-through cannot make the recovery action unreachable.
- Cancel preserves recovery; a successful snip restores the normal live view.
- No private surfaces are captured for tests or documentation.

Completion evidence:
- scripts\build.ps1 -Test passed Release /W4 /WX, 18 pure cases and 36 native
  checks, including real recovery hit testing, pointer/keyboard selection,
  cancellation, minimum bounds, click-through override and return to live view.
- docs\assets\recovery-pane.png is the inspected actual native fixture surface.
- README and user/verification guides document recovery and its input behavior.
- No normal-view title bar, toolbar, private capture or publication was added.

Completion log:
- 2026-11-06: User showed an unactionable source-resized message and requested
  an in-place way to snip again. Scoped recovery to resized/closed sources.
- 2026-11-06: Added drawn native recovery action, client hit testing, press/release
  capture, Enter/Space and temporary click-through suspension. Cancellation
  restores unavailable placeholders rather than restarting invalid/dead sources.
